= The Return

The president takes the oath again, with unified control of Congress and a Supreme Court inclined to defer on executive power. In the first days come dozens of executive orders, mass pardons of January 6th defendants, a sweeping reshuffling of the civil service, and a campaign to shrink the federal government. The party is in the minority in both chambers.

- @court: Sue first. Ask questions later.
- @regroup: Take time to regroup.
- @fight: Fight everywhere, immediately.

@court
subtitle: Institutional.
on-arrival: stability += 3; funds -= 1 if funds > 0; media_trust += 1

State attorneys general and civil-society groups file suit after suit. Some injunctions stand. Many do not.

@regroup
subtitle: Avoids a reflexive fight.
on-arrival: unity += 3; enthusiasm -= 2; capital += 1

We do an honest post-mortem. The base is impatient.

@fight
subtitle: Energy.
on-arrival: enthusiasm += 4; prog_dissent -= 3; stability += 1; capital -= 1 if capital > 0

We make noise. Parts of the base love it. Moderates ask what the plan is.
